# Accepted findings — each needs a reason and a review date (docs/review-checklist.md).

# decode-uri-component 0.2.2 (DoS on crafted percent-encoding), via expo-router -> query-string@7.
# The fixed 0.5.x is ESM-only and breaks query-string@7's require(), which breaks app routing.
# Exposure: client-side only — it parses the viewer's own URL in their own browser/app; no server uses it.
# Revisit when expo-router moves off query-string@7. Review by 2027-02-01.
CVE-2026-118664

# @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger 1.30.1 (DoS on a malformed uber-trace-id header), via @traceroot-ai/traceroot
# -> @opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node 1.x. TraceRoot's SDK pins OpenTelemetry 1.x; the fixed 2.x does not fit it.
# Exposure: none in deployed services — TraceRoot is a devDependency of ty-copilot (absent from the `pnpm deploy
# --prod` image), runs only on the laptop for test traffic (TRACEROOT_ENABLED, refused in live), and the Jaeger
# propagator is only used when OTEL_PROPAGATORS includes jaeger, which nothing sets.
# Revisit when @traceroot-ai/traceroot moves to OpenTelemetry 2.x. Review by 2027-02-01.
CVE-2026-59892
